      "content": "\\begin{table}[htbp]\\centering\\scriptsize\n\\def\\sym#1{\\ifmmode^{#1}\\else\\(^{#1}\\)\\fi}\n\\caption{\\textbf{Instrumental Variable Regressions}}\n\\label{iv}\n\n\\noindent{\\justifying{This table presents the results of the instrumental variable regressions using the Two-Stage Least Squares (2SLS) method to address potential endogeneity for a sample of Chinese A-share listed firms from 2003 to 2023. Columns (1) through (3) report the first-stage regression results, where the dependent variable is \\textsl{PTC}. Columns (4) through (6) report the second-stage results, where the dependent variable is \\textsl{Institution}. Three policy shocks are used as instrumental variables: \\textsl{TechFin} (Columns 1 and 4), defined as a dummy variable equal to one if the city is selected as a pilot zone for combining technology and finance; \\textsl{Broadband} (Columns 2 and 5), defined as a dummy variable equal to one if the city is selected as a ``Broadband China'' demonstration city; and \\textsl{Court} (Columns 3 and 6), defined as a dummy variable equal to one if an intellectual property court or tribunal is established in the city. The main explanatory variable (endogenous variable) is \\textsl{PTC} (a dummy variable that equals one if the city where the firm is located has established a patent trading center in or before year $t$). The dependent variable \\textsl{Institution} is defined as the ratio of the number of shares held by institutional investors to the total number of shares. Other control variables are aligned with Table \\ref{baseline}. All regressions include firm and year fixed effects. The robust $t$-statistics clustered by the firm are reported in parentheses. The Kleibergen-Paap rk Wald F-statistics are reported to test for weak instruments. The detailed variable definitions are presented in Table \\ref{definition}. ***, **, and * denote the significance at the 1\\%, 5\\%, and 10\\% levels, respectively.\\par}}\n\\bigskip\n\n\\begin{tabularx}{\\textwidth}{lYYYYYYYY@{}}\n\\toprule\n\n                &\\multicolumn{3}{c}{First Stage}                         &\\multicolumn{3}{c}{Second Stage}                        \\\\\\cmidrule(lr){2-4}\\cmidrule(lr){5-7}\n                &\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(1)}&\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(2)}&\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(3)}&\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(4)}&\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(5)}&\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(6)}\\\\\n                &\\multicolumn{1}{c}{PTC}&\\multicolumn{1}{c}{PTC}&\\multicolumn{1}{c}{PTC}&\\multicolumn{1}{c}{Institution}&\\multicolumn{1}{c}{Institution}&\\multicolumn{1}{c}{Institution}\\\\\n\\hline\\\\\nTechFin         &   0.1399\\sym{***}&                  &                  &                  &                  &                  \\\\\n                &  (12.53)         &                  &                  &                  &                  &                  \\\\\nBroadband       &                  &   0.0708\\sym{***}&                  &                  &                  &                  \\\\\n                &                  &  (10.12)         &                  &                  &                  &                  \\\\\nCourt           &                  &                  &   0.0644\\sym{***}&                  &                  &                  \\\\\n                &                  &                  &  (14.23)         &                  &                  &                  \\\\\nPTC          &                  &                  &                  &  -1.2057\\sym{***}&  -1.3280\\sym{***}&  -1.2035\\sym{***}\\\\\n                &                  &                  &                  &  (-4.89)         &  (-3.37)         &  (-3.41)         \\\\\nSize            &   0.0079\\sym{*}  &   0.0072         &   0.0069         &   0.0047         &  -0.0149         &  -0.0158         \\\\\n                &   (1.71)         &   (1.61)         &   (1.55)         &   (0.26)         &  (-0.84)         &  (-0.91)         \\\\\nBalance         &   0.0118