      "content": "\\begin{table}[htbp]\\centering\\scriptsize\n\\def\\sym#1{\\ifmmode^{#1}\\else\\(^{#1}\\)\\fi}\n\\caption{\\textbf{Alternative Variable Definitions}}\n\\label{measures}\n\n\\noindent{\\justifying{This table presents the association between local patent trading infrastructure and institutional ownership for a sample of Chinese A-share listed firms from 2003 to 2023 using alternative variable definitions. The dependent variables are \\textsl{LnInstitution} (the natural logarithm of one plus the total institutional shareholding ratio) in Columns (1)–(2), \\textsl{ProfInst} (the combined shareholding ratio of mutual funds, securities brokers, and trusts) in Columns (3)–(4), and \\textsl{Fund} (the shareholding ratio of mutual funds) in Columns (5)–(6). The main explanatory variable is \\textsl{PTC}, a dummy variable that equals 1 if the city where the firm is located has established a patent trading center by year $t$, and 0 otherwise. Other control variables include \\textsl{Size} (the natural logarithm of total assets), \\textsl{Balance} (the degree of equity balance), \\textsl{ROA} (the ratio of net income to total assets), \\textsl{Tobinq} (the market-to-book ratio), \\textsl{Age} (the natural logarithm of firm age), \\textsl{Cash} (net cash flow divided by total assets), \\textsl{Indept} (the percentage of independent directors), \\textsl{Top1} (the shareholding ratio of the largest shareholder), \\textsl{Dual} (a dummy variable for chairman and CEO duality), \\textsl{FinDev} (city financial development), \\textsl{Innov} (city innovation potential), \\textsl{Open} (city openness), and \\textsl{Gov} (government intervention). All regressions include firm and city fixed effects, alongside year or industry $\\times$ year fixed effects. The robust $t$-statistics clustered by the firm are reported in parentheses. The detailed variable definitions are presented in Table S1. ***, **, and * denote the significance at the 1\\%, 5\\%, and 10\\% levels, respectively.\\par}}\n\\bigskip\n\n\\begin{tabularx}{\\textwidth}{lYYYYYYYY@{}}\n\\toprule\n\n                &\\multicolumn{2}{c}{LnInstitution}    &\\multicolumn{2}{c}{ProfInst}         &\\multicolumn{2}{c}{Fund}             \\\\\\cmidrule(lr){2-3}\\cmidrule(lr){4-5}\\cmidrule(lr){6-7}\n                &\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(1)}         &\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(2)}         &\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(3)}         &\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(4)}         &\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(5)}         &\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(6)}         \\\\\n\\hline\\\\\nPTC             &  -0.0383\\sym{***}&  -0.0342\\sym{***}&  -0.0162\\sym{***}&  -0.0145\\sym{**} &  -0.0089\\sym{*}  &  -0.0087         \\\\\n                &  (-3.34)         &  (-2.92)         &  (-2.65)         &  (-2.33)         &  (-1.70)         &  (-1.64)         \\\\\nSize            &  -0.0069         &  -0.0138\\sym{**} &   0.0188\\sym{***}&   0.0199\\sym{***}&   0.0140\\sym{***}&   0.0147\\sym{***}\\\\\n                &  (-1.30)         &  (-2.52)         &   (9.48)         &  (10.11)         &   (8.52)         &   (9.13)         \\\\\nBalance         &   0.2806\\sym{***}&   0.2820\\sym{***}&   0.0387\\sym{***}&   0.0356\\sym{***}&   0.0236\\sym{***}&   0.0202\\sym{***}\\\\\n                &  (31.20)         &  (31.61)         &  (12.11)         &  (11.11)         &   (9.34)         &   (8.03)         \\\\\nROA             &   0.4999\\sym{***}&   0.4523\\sym{***}&   0.2484\\sym{***}&   0.2294\\sym{***}&   0.2389\\sym{***}&   0.2213\\sym{***}\\\\\n                &  (17.04)         &  (15.31)         &  (21.65)         &  (19.86)         &  (24.34)         &  (22.86)         \\\\\nTobinq          &  -0.0445\\sym{***}&  -0.0511\\sym{***}&   0.0143\\sym{***}&   0.0134\\sym{***}&   0.0155\\sym{***}&   0.0147\\sym{***}\\\\\n                & (-17.68)         & (-19.75)         &  (14.88)         &  (13.86)         &  (17.66)         &  (16.64)         \\\\\nAge             &  -0.0269\\sym{*}  &  -0.0248\\sym{**} &   0.0136         &   0.0111  