      "path": "template/sampling.tex",
      "encoding": "utf8",
      "content": "\\begin{table}[htbp]\\centering\\scriptsize\n\\def\\sym#1{\\ifmmode^{#1}\\else\\(^{#1}\\)\\fi}\n\\caption{\\textbf{Alternative Sampling Criteria}}\n\\label{sampling}\n\n\\noindent{\\justifying{This table reports the robustness check results of the association between local patent trading infrastructure and institutional ownership for a sample of Chinese A-share listed firms from 2003 to 2023 using alternative sampling criteria. To examine the effect on market-oriented entities, state-owned enterprises (SOEs) are excluded in Column (1). Due to the impact of extreme market events (the 2008 financial crisis, the 2015 stock market crash, and the COVID-19 pandemic), samples in 2008, 2015, and 2020-2022 are excluded in Column (2). Column (3) excludes non-high-tech firms to focus on innovation-intensive industries. High-tech firms are identified based on the CSRC (2012) industry classification, including sectors such as Pharmaceuticals (C27), Specialized/Transport Equipment (C35-C37), Electronics and Computing (C38-C40), and IT Services (Category I). Results remain robust within this innovation-active subsample. Column (4) excludes firms listed for less than three years to avoid the mechanical impact of IPO lock-up periods. The dependent variable is \\textsl{Institution}, defined as the ratio of the number of shares held by institutional investors to the total number of shares at the year-end. The main explanatory variable is \\textsl{PTC} (a dummy variable that equals one if the city where the firm is located has established a patent trading center in or before year $t$, and zero otherwise). Other control variables are aligned with Table \\ref{baseline}. All regressions include firm, year, and city fixed effects. The robust $t$-statistics clustered by the firm are reported in parentheses. The detailed variable definitions are presented in Table \\ref{definition}. ***, **, and * denote the significance at the 1\\%, 5\\%, and 10\\% levels, respectively.\\par}}\n\\bigskip\n\n\\begin{tabularx}{\\textwidth}{lYYYYYYYY@{}}\n\\toprule\n\n                &\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(1)}&\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(2)}&\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(3)}&\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(4)}\\\\\n                &\\multicolumn{1}{c}{Excluding SOEs}&\\multicolumn{1}{c}{Excluding Crisis Years}&\\multicolumn{1}{c}{Excluding Non-High-Tech}&\\multicolumn{1}{c}{Excluding Lock-up Period}\\\\\n\\hline\\\\\nPTC          &  -0.1610\\sym{**} &  -0.1661\\sym{***}&  -0.2045\\sym{***}&  -0.1915\\sym{***}\\\\\n                &  (-2.51)         &  (-3.87)         &  (-2.75)         &  (-4.21)         \\\\\nSize            &  -0.0987\\sym{***}&  -0.0067         &  -0.0867\\sym{***}&   0.0878\\sym{***}\\\\\n                &  (-4.88)         &  (-0.36)         &  (-3.23)         &   (5.49)         \\\\\nBalance         &   0.4859\\sym{***}&   0.6063\\sym{***}&   0.4685\\sym{***}&   0.5016\\sym{***}\\\\\n                &  (15.97)         &  (21.47)         &  (13.02)         &  (21.92)         \\\\\nROA             &   1.0790\\sym{***}&   1.0603\\sym{***}&   1.0092\\sym{***}&   0.5231\\sym{***}\\\\\n                &  (10.94)         &   (9.42)         &   (8.67)         &   (7.05)         \\\\\nTobinq          &  -0.1587\\sym{***}&  -0.1301\\sym{***}&  -0.1642\\sym{***}&  -0.0129\\sym{**} \\\\\n                & (-16.72)         & (-13.40)         & (-16.08)         &  (-2.24)         \\\\\nAge             &  -0.0289         &   0.0215         &  -0.1171\\sym{***}&   0.1047\\sym{**} \\\\\n                &  (-0.49)         &   (0.54)         &  (-2.59)         &   (2.28)         \\\\\nCash            &   0.0083         &   0.1142         &   0.1575         &   0.0294         \\\\\n                &   (0.10)         &   (1.35)         &   (1.48)         &   (0.46)         \\\\\nIndept          &  -0.4531\\sym{**} &  -0.3015         &  -0.0518         &  -0.2801\\sym{*}  \\\\\n                &  (-2.21)         &  (-1.56)         &  (-0.23)         &  (-1.88)         \\\\\nTop1  