      "path": "template/specification.tex",
      "encoding": "utf8",
      "content": "\\begin{table}[htbp]\\centering\\scriptsize\n\\def\\sym#1{\\ifmmode^{#1}\\else\\(^{#1}\\)\\fi}\n\\caption{\\textbf{Model Specification}}\n\\label{specification}\n\n\\noindent{\\justifying{This table reports the robustness check results using high-dimensional interactive fixed effects for a sample of Chinese A-share listed firms from 2003 to 2023. The dependent variable is \\textsl{Institution}, defined as the ratio of the number of shares held by institutional investors to the total number of shares at the year-end. The main explanatory variable is \\textsl{PTC} (a dummy variable that equals one if the city where the firm is located has established a patent trading center in or before year $t$, and zero otherwise). Control variables include \\textsl{Size} (natural logarithm of total assets), \\textsl{Balance} (degree of equity balance, calculated as the sum of shareholdings of the 2nd to 10th largest shareholders divided by the shareholding of the largest shareholder), \\textsl{ROA} (the ratio of net income to total assets), \\textsl{Tobinq} (the ratio of the market value of assets to the book value of assets), \\textsl{Age} (natural logarithm of the number of years since the firm's establishment), \\textsl{Cash} (net cash flow from operating activities divided by total assets), \\textsl{Indept} (the ratio of the number of independent directors to total board members), \\textsl{Top1} (the shareholding ratio of the biggest shareholder), \\textsl{Dual} (a dummy variable that equals one if the same individual concurrently holds the positions of chairman and general manager and zero otherwise), \\textsl{FinDev} (city financial development, measured as the ratio of the balance of loans of financial institutions to regional GDP), \\textsl{Innov} (city innovation potential, measured as the ratio of science and technology expenditure to local general budget expenditure), \\textsl{Open} (city openness, measured as the ratio of actually utilized Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) to regional GDP), and \\textsl{Gov} (government intervention, measured as the ratio of local general budget expenditure to regional GDP). All regressions include firm, year, and city fixed effects. Column (1) further controls for industry $\\times$ year fixed effects. Column (2) further controls for province $\\times$ year fixed effects. Column (3) simultaneously controls for both industry $\\times$ year and province $\\times$ year fixed effects. The robust $t$-statistics clustered by the firm are reported in parentheses. ***, **, and * denote the significance at the 1\\%, 5\\%, and 10\\% levels, respectively.\\par}}\n\\bigskip\n\n\\begin{tabularx}{\\textwidth}{lYYYYYYYY@{}}\n\\toprule\n\n                &\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(1)}         &\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(2)}         &\\multicolumn{1}{c}{(3)}         \\\\\n\\hline\\\\\nPTC          &  -0.1467\\sym{***}&  -0.1260\\sym{**} &  -0.1243\\sym{**} \\\\\n                &  (-3.44)         &  (-2.18)         &  (-2.25)         \\\\\nSize            &  -0.0518\\sym{***}&  -0.0314\\sym{*}  &  -0.0599\\sym{***}\\\\\n                &  (-3.06)         &  (-1.95)         &  (-3.60)         \\\\\nBalance         &   0.5939\\sym{***}&   0.5809\\sym{***}&   0.5949\\sym{***}\\\\\n                &  (24.26)         &  (23.59)         &  (24.40)         \\\\\nROA             &   0.9733\\sym{***}&   1.0843\\sym{***}&   0.9656\\sym{***}\\\\\n                &  (11.03)         &  (12.28)         &  (11.03)         \\\\\nTobinq          &  -0.1528\\sym{***}&  -0.1338\\sym{***}&  -0.1559\\sym{***}\\\\\n                & (-19.01)         & (-17.09)         & (-19.35)         \\\\\nAge             &  -0.0267         &  -0.0933\\sym{***}&  -0.0896\\sym{***}\\\\\n                &  (-0.90)         &  (-2.88)         &  (-2.92)         \\\\\nCash            &   0.0374         &   0.0573         &   0.0199         \\\\\n                &   (0.54)         &   (0.83)         &   (0.29)         \\\\\nIndept          &  -0.3450\\sym{**} &  -0.4110\\sym{**} &  -0.4115\\sym{***}\\\\\n                &  (-2.16)         &  (-2.54)         &  (-2.61)         \\\\\nTop1            &   3.8145\\sym{***}&   3.7251\\sym{***}&   3.8390\\sym{***}\\\\\n                &  (28.89)         &  (29.53)         &  (29.56)         \\\\\nDual            &   0.0390\\sym{**} &   0.0464\\sym{***}&   0.0393\\sym{**} \\\\\n                &   (2.44)         &   (2.81)         &   (2.44)         \\\\\nFinDev          &   0.0624\\sym{**} &  -0.0217         &  -0.0443         \\\\\n                &   (2.33)         &  (-0.49)         &  (-1.00)         \\\\\nInnov           &  -2.0371\\sym{***}&  -1.2859\\sym{*}  &  -1.5232\\sym{**} \\\\\n                &  (-4.01)         &  (-1.83)         &  (-2.21)         \\\\\nOpen            &   0.7072\\sym{*}  &  -0.3219         &   0.2812         \\\\\n                &   (1.69)         &  (-0.42)         &   (0.41)         \\\\\nGov             &  -0.3219         &   0.4176         &   0.2527         \\\\\n                &  (-1.11)         &   (0.92)         &   (0.58)         \\\\\n\\hline\nObservations    &   45,552         &   45,654         &   45,552         \\\\\nFirm FE         &      Yes         &      Yes         &      Yes         \\\\\nYear FE         &      Yes         &      Yes         &      Yes         \\\\\nInd $\\times$ Year FE&      Yes         &       No         &      Yes         \\\\\nProv $\\times$ Year FE&       No         &      Yes         &      Yes         \\\\\nAdjusted $ R^2$ &     0.59         &     0.58         &     0.60         \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabularx}\n\\end{table}\n"
