      "content": "\\begin{table}[htbp]\\centering\\scriptsize\n\\def\\sym#1{\\ifmmode^{#1}\\else\\(^{#1}\\)\\fi}\n\\caption{\\textbf{Variable Definitions}}\n\\label{definition}\n\n\\begin{tabular}{p{2.0cm}p{13.5cm}}\n\\toprule\nVariable       &        Definition\\\\\n\\hline\\\\\nInstitution   & The ratio of the number of shares held by institutional investors to the total number of shares at the year-end.\\\\\nPTC   & A dummy variable that equals one if the city where the firm is located has established a patent trading center (PTC) in or before year $t$, and zero otherwise.\\\\\nSize   & Natural logarithm of total assets. \\\\\nBalance   & Degree of equity balance, calculated as the sum of shareholdings of the 2nd to 10th largest shareholders divided by the shareholding of the largest shareholder. \\\\\nROA   & The ratio of net income to total assets. \\\\\nTobinq   & The ratio of the market value of assets to the book value of assets. \\\\\nAge   & Natural logarithm of the number of years since the firm's establishment.\\\\\nCash   & Net cash flow from operating activities divided by total assets. \\\\\nIndept   & The ratio of the number of independent directors to total board members. \\\\\nTop1   & The shareholding ratio of the biggest shareholder. \\\\\nSOE   & A dummy variable that equals one if the ultimate controller is the government or a state-owned enterprise, and zero otherwise. \\\\\nDual   & a dummy variable that equals one if the same individual concurrently holds the positions of chairman and general manager and zero otherwise. \\\\\nFinDev   & City financial development, measured as the ratio of the balance of loans of financial institutions to regional GDP. \\\\\nInnov   & City innovation potential, measured as the ratio of science and technology expenditure to local general budget expenditure. \\\\\nOpen   & City openness, measured as the ratio of actually utilized Foreign Direct Investment (FDI) to regional GDP. \\\\\nGov   & Government intervention, measured as the ratio of local general budget expenditure to regional GDP. \\\\\nTechFin   & A dummy variable equal to one if the city is approved as a pilot zone for combining technology and finance, and zero otherwise. \\\\\nBroadband   & a dummy variable that equals one if a city is approved as a “Broadband China” pilot city in a given year and thereafter, and zero otherwise. \\\\\nCourt   & A dummy variable equal to one if an intellectual property court or tribunal is established in the city, and zero otherwise. \\\\\nJunkPatents   & Strategic innovators identified as firms with a non-invention patent application ratio greater than 90\\%. \\\\\nRealInnovation   & Substantive innovators identified as firms with a non-invention patent application ratio less than 50\\%. \\\\\nDebtPatience & Calculated as the ratio of relational debt to total liabilities. Relational debt aggregates Notes Payable, Long-term Loans, Bonds Payable, and Long-term Payables, representing formal financing sources secured through explicit credit contracts and long-term relationships rather than spontaneous operating activities. \\\\\nEquityPatience   & Measured as the stability of institutional ownership, calculated as the ratio of the institutional shareholding percentage to its standard deviation over the past three years. \\\\\nDeltaCash   & Annual change in cash and cash equivalents over total assets. \\\\\nIntCoverage   & Earnings before interest and taxes divided by interest expense. \\\\\nLev   & The total leverage ratio, calculated as the ratio of total liabilities to total assets. \\\\\nMaturity   & The debt maturity structure, calculated as the ratio of long-term loans to total liabilities. \\\\\nLnLongloan   & The absolute volume of long-term credit, measured as the natural logarithm of one plus long-term loans. \\\\\nLTLeverage   & The long-term debt leverage ratio, calculated as the ratio of long-term loans to total assets. \\\\\nCod   & The cost of debt financing, measured as the ratio of total financial expenses to total liabilities at the end of the fiscal year. \\\\\nTenure   & Institutional holding tenure, calculated as the average number of consecutive years that institutional investors have appeared in the top ten shareholders list. \\\\\nAbsDA   & Accrual earnings management, measured as the absolute value of discretionary accruals estimated using the Modified Jones Model. \\\\\nPerks   & Managerial perks, measured as the ratio of management expenses (minus the total compensation of directors, supervisors, and senior executives) to total operating revenue. \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\end{table}\n\n\\begin{table}[htbp]\\centering\\scriptsize\n\\def\\sym#1{\\ifmmode^{#1}\\else\\(^{#1}\\)\\fi}\n\\begin{tabular}{p{2.0cm} p{13cm}}\n\\toprule\nPatentStock   & A dummy variable equal to one if the firm possesses granted patents, and zero otherwise. \\\\\nATO   & Asset turnover ratio (Revenue divided by total assets), used to measure operating efficiency. \\\\\nZ-score   & Altman Z-score used to proxy for financial distress risk, calculated based on the firm's liquidity, profitability, leverage, and solvency. \\\\\nTurnover   & Annual stock turnover rate, used to proxy for market speculation or turnover pressure. \\\\\nMarketShare   & Market share, defined as firm revenue divided by total industry revenue. \\\\\nTradingCapital   & Combined ownership of mutual funds, securities brokers, and trusts. \\\\\nPatientCapital   & Combined ownership of QFIIs, insurance companies, and social security funds. \\\\\nStrategicCapital   & Combined ownership of banks, finance companies, and non-financial corporate blockholders. \\\\\nInvestment   & The firm's investment rate, measured as cash paid for acquiring fixed assets and intangible assets divided by lagged total assets. \\\\\nStrategicMix   & The strategic investment allocation ratio, defined as R\\&D expenses divided by the sum of R\\&D and capital expenditure. \\\\\nLnInstitution   & The natural logarithm of one plus the total institutional shareholding ratio at the year-end. \\\\\nProfInst   & The combined shareholding ratio of mutual funds, securities brokers, and trust companies relative to floating A-shares. \\\\\nFund   & The shareholding ratio of mutual funds relative to floating A-shares. \\\\\nRelaxation   & a dummy variable that equals one if the price limit on the firm’s trading board is relaxed, and zero otherwise. (ChiNext in 2020 and Sci-Tech innovation board in 2019). \\\\\nPatentReform   & A dummy variable that equals one if the patent approval system reform is in the city where the firm is located, and zero otherwise. \\\\\n\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabular}\n\\end{table}"
    }
  ]
}